# Plan

This is the board — the team's work on the workbook, as data. It proves a claim that
sounds wrong at first: **declarative is not immutable.** The same document you read is
the one the agents write back into; tasks move from `:todo` to `:done` *in this file*.
The document is the database.

A task is a **resource** — its shape and its rows in one place. It renders by default,
so this list *is* the board on the page:

resource Task do
  title   :text
  status  :todo | :doing | :done
  owner   :text                # nil until an agent claims it
  ref     :atom                # the unit this task is about

  seed [
    %{title: "Wire enrich → CRM API",         status: :done,  owner: "ana", ref: :enrich},
    %{title: "Tune scoring weights",          status: :doing, owner: "ana", ref: :score},
    %{title: "Forecast next-quarter pipe",    status: :todo,  owner: nil,   ref: :forecast},
    %{title: "Draft outreach for hot leads",  status: :todo,  owner: nil,   ref: :analyst}
  ]
end

`owner` must resolve to a real person or agent; `ref` points at the unit the task is
about — both checked at the weave gate.

Two tasks have no owner — they're unclaimed. Next: how agents claim work without
trampling each other ([[Claim, lock & fence]]), and [[A full harness]] in one file.
